{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1795820448,"nonce":"Vsa0EGgLCzjWi3YfFnP4y8Mz698=","title":"Documentation workflow: the book example check fails offline on wgpu-hal","message":"The \"Check book application examples\" step of the Build Book job fails with\n`failed to download wgpu-hal v26.0.5` and `--offline was specified`\n(run 46075500373 at 6e950814, both attempts).\n\n`scripts/check_book_examples.py` writes a crate outside the workspace and\nchecks it with `--offline`. The workspace patches crates.io's `wgpu-hal` to\n`third_party/wgpu-hal`, and that patch does not reach the temporary crate, so\nit needs the registry's copy, which nothing in the workspace uses.\n\nIt passed while an older cargo cache still held the crate. Rust 1.100.1 on the\nrunners changed the cache key. The first wrapper shard saved the new cache,\nwithout the registry copy, and the Build Book job restored it. Re-running\ndoes not help, because the saved cache is found by its exact key.\n\nReproduced locally with a cargo home that has every registry crate but\n`wgpu-hal-26.0.5`.","files":null}]}